/steam/apps/40330/ss_30d7889d94e9c91616c727c9c093f4a757351b56.1920x1080.jpg?t=1792657526"}],"movies":[],"genres":["Adventure"],"features":["Single-player","Family Sharing"],"platforms":{"windows":true,"mac":false,"linux":false},"controller":null,"dev":["Animation Arts"],"pub":["Animation Arts"],"released":"Oct 29, 2009","meta":null,"langs":["English","French","German","Italian"],"min":[["OS","Windows"],["Processor","500 MHz Intel Pentium III or AMD Equivalent CPU"],["Memory","128 MB RAM"],["Graphics","16 MB DirectX compatible graphics card"],["Hard Drive","2 GB hard disk space"],["Sound","DirectX compatible sound card"]],"rec":[],"deck":2,"blurb":"Secret Files: Tunguska is a point-and-click mystery built around the real Tunguska event of 1908, when a huge explosion flattened forest across a remote part of Siberia. In the game, Nina Kalenkov finds her father, a scientist who studied the event, has vanished from his office, and her search with his colleague Max Gruber pulls them into a mystery that spans several countries.\n\nYou explore, collect and combine objects, and question characters to move the investigation along. It is a single-player adventure with a measured pace and no action, suited to players who enjoy classic puzzle-based adventures with a historical hook."}}